    "created_at": "2016-09-07T23:45:16Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-09-07T23:45:16Z",
    "body": "FYI per https://html.spec.whatwg.org/commit-snapshots/c9e804f04d03a0658bfa689cb0f368a4d2e37936#execute-the-script-block this has been in the spec since before I started messing with script elements for `<script type=\"module\">` and ES integration and such. So at least this isn't some accidental new addition.\n\nI don't have a strong preference about whether we should have this or not. I guess I'd feel bad about changing the spec if IE/Edge faithfully implemented it on purpose. Whereas if the spec just chose the 1/4 behavior at the time, I'm happy to say that this hasn't gotten traction and flip to the 3/4 behavior.\n\nIt would be helpful to find out of there's any history here or if someone presented a compelling argument for inline script tags firing load events that caused @Hixie to add this back in the day. Some quick Googling doesn't turn anything up immediately.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
