    "created_at": "2016-09-12T19:11:19Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-09-12T19:11:19Z",
    "body": "Asking around authors seem fairly split on whether this is a good idea or not. So I am inclined to go with the 3/4 majority. Let's make sure no implementers want to go with the current spec before we churn though.\n\n@cdumez, @rniwa; @dominiccooney, @tkent-google; @travisleithead; @bzbarsky: currently the spec and Edge fire \"load\" events for inline scripts (no src attribute). We are thinking we should align the spec (and web platform tests) with the 3/4 majority, but want to make sure you are OK with that. If you could sign off explicitly that would be very helpful.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
